{"id": "EUVD-2026-102474", "enisaUuid": "5a80a7c6-8628-3cdd-acce-8aa64033d4a8", "description": "BMC Helix Network Management on-prem 26.3.00 before 26.3.01 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to log in as the local administrator with any password when SAML single sign-on is configured. Attackers can submit the administrator username with an arbitrary password on the web login page to obtain a SuperAdmin session, modify device credentials, run device commands, and alter audit records.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T10:46:34", "baseScore": 9.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H", "references": ["https://docs.helixops.ai/bin/IT-Operations-Management/Operations-Management/BMC-Helix-Network-Management/NetworkManagement/Release-Notes/On-prem-Release-Notes/BMC-Helix-Network-Management-26-3-01-On-prem-Release-Notes/", "https://github.com/cybliminal/cve-2026-111283-bmc-helix-network-management-local-administrator-any-password", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bmc-helix-network-management-before-26.3.01-authentication-bypass-via-saml-configuration"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111283", "GHSA-w2gx-x7ww-hgvm"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.53, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "21428a13-4971-3dab-bc7f-0f777cfa2719", "product": {"name": "BMC Helix Network Management", "vendor": {"name": "BMC Helix"}}, "product_version": "26.3.00 <26.3.01"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d9294ec5-984e-3c99-bd62-03d08cf2d85a", "vendor": {"name": "BMC Helix"}}], "isExploited": false}